A||||3||StuGood||TV Cable Setup||||5||
Z||000000||StuGood||09-13-2000||03:15 PM||||When the TV cable is adjusted properly on an auto Fiero, is it supposed to pull the thingy  in the trans. out to the limit of its travel at WOT?  Is that the "goal" of the adjustment  procedure outlined in the service manuals?<P>I can read the manual, so I'm more or less  familiar with the procedure.  What I'd like to know is, what's the end result supposed to look like?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-13-2000||10:43 PM||||sort of. you set the cable as described in the manual. Then turn the thottle to WOT. (Do this in the engine bay NOT with the accelerator pedal!) The sleave will ratchet in as you turn the throttle.<P>You have to be carefull with that adjustment not to pull the sleave out too far. <P>BEFORE you turn the throttle..... The adjust button should look the same as when you started. If the button is sticking up above the casing or looks slanted then push the button and slide the sleave back in a little.<P>The cable should settle itself at WOT. Problem is it takes a pretty good amount of force to make the cable adjust itself. ((This is why they tell you NOT to push the accelerator to do this. You'll break the accelerator cable or bend the pedle hardware.))<P>If you can't turn the throttle all the way to WOT then go as far as you can. Then adjust the cable by hand a couple teeth at a time untill you can reach WOT.<P>Even tho the cable is suposed to be self adjusting I've found you sometimes have to tweek them a couple teeth one way or the other by hand to get the shifting just right. (This applies to more vehicles than Fiero. My dodge caravan was the same way.)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||80's BOY||09-14-2000||12:01 PM||||would i lose performance if this isn't adjusted right?? i've never even messed with my TV cable even after the rebuild. what are the symptoms if it not adjusted correctly??<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||theogre||09-14-2000||10:46 PM||||depends how far off it is. Most people wouldn't notice a couple teeth off. <P>Very much off it can sigificantly screw up shifting. depends wich way its off and how far. If its way off the tranny will eather shift real soft or shifting will be delayed and hard. Niether one is good.<P>messing with the engine often won't alter the TV cable adjustment unless you mess with the button on the cable. when the motor is reassembled everything pretty much ends up where it started. (If it doesn't something is way wrong.)<P>Once the cable is set it should rarely need to be messed with. A slight adjustment maybe to accomodate wear. of course if the tranny is dissassembled or the cable is replaced it will likely need adjustment. There's not much to go wrong with it.||||reg||1
